# felix-alert bus — topic env-file template.
#
# Deployed (out-of-band, NEVER committed) to:
#   /home/claude/.config/felix/alert-bus/env   (mode 0600, owner claude:claude)
#
# The operator mints a NEW high-entropy ntfy.sh topic (do not reuse the
# felix-deployer or health-check topics) and fills the value below on office2.
# The topic id is a secret: knowing it lets a passive listener read alert bodies
# (which carry error text + paths). It is never committed to the repo (C-002
# exception) — this template ships only the empty placeholder.
#
# Consumers resolve FELIX_ALERT_NTFY_TOPIC via:
#   - systemd EnvironmentFile= on felix-deployer.service, felix-health-check.service,
#     and agent-prompt-sync.service (systemd context); and
#   - scripts/common/alert_bus.sh sourcing this file directly (cron context, e.g.
#     the security-monitor audit.sh which inherits no systemd EnvironmentFile).
FELIX_ALERT_NTFY_TOPIC=
